Track 3: Airlock Red Rover
- Story & Context: On the summer solstice of 2024, an unmapped Azores repeater blew its pressure seals, venting an ear-splitting melodic frequency through Horta Harbor that sent thousands of tourists and fishermen spilling onto the sun-baked docks. The sound of high-voltage industrial pulses and warm vibraphone chords vibrated the hulls of sixty wooden whaling boats, causing harbor-side fruit vendors to abandon their stalls as entire crowds began a chaotic, laughing charge through customs security barriers. Divers surfacing from the harbor basin climbed straight onto the piers without removing their fins, joining the running human chain while singing over the pier’s PA system: "Step over di cable, jump di whole Atlantic wide!" By twilight, the harbor had dissolved into an open-air carnival of chilled passionfruit rum, high-vis work vests, and shuddering coastal sound systems.
